</ul><h1>Carry Styles</h1><p><strong>The task</strong></p>
<p>Flying home for the holidays</p>
<p><strong>The bad news</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Due to it being a peak travel time, and also due to high fuel costs, your round-trip ticket’s price looks eerily similar to a rent payment. And your destination is not some tropical locale; it’s your childhood home. Welp, there goes that vacation you had planned.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>All flights home leave at either 5:30am or 11:30pm. What’s more, after choosing a time, you will find that the cost you saw before, already exorbitantly high, was actually some sort of super budget offering that includes almost nothing, and you will have to pay even more if you want to experience such luxuries as: choosing your seat and bringing a carry-on bag with you.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>At the gate, the agent on duty will make an announcement that, due to overbooking, they’re looking for people to defer travel in exchange for a voucher. The agent will make this announcement without a shred of embarrassment at the fact that, apparently, the airline company doesn’t know how to count. The voucher will seem appealing at first, until you remember the cost of your own ticket and realize the amount offered <em>might</em> just cover the tax on your next trip.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>At your layover, you will buy a beer, a little holiday indulgence. The bill will show that you owe $22. You will look around for a food item that has been delivered to you by accident before realizing this is, in fact, the cost of only the beer. What’s more, it will put you into the uncanny valley of brain fog: not so tired that you can fall asleep, but just sleepy enough that you can’t focus enough to read.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>On your second flight, they will ask to check your bag to its destination due to limited space in the overhead bins. This will be fine enough, but when it comes time to collect the bag at baggage claim, you will find the conveyor belt crowded with people, rushing to stand in everyone’s way, as if their positioning will somehow impact the order in which the bags come out.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>The good news</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>You bought a new duffel and backpack from Meh before the holidays for a good price, so at least your bags are nice enough.</li>
</ul>